   "reasoning_summary": "C11H13N has DoU 6, consistent with a benzene ring (4) plus a nitrile (2); the C\u2261N appears at 117.4 (id 9). Only 8 13C signals for 11 carbons implies a symmetric 1,2,4,6-substituted ring: four aromatic C (ids 5-8), two CH3 types (ids 10, 11) and a CH2 (id 12). The 1H spectrum fits this: one ArH signal at 6.89 (id 1), ArCH2CN at 3.59 (id 2), and ortho/para ArCH3 at 2.35/2.26 (ids 3, 4). The shielded CH2CN carbon at 17.4 ppm is characteristic of benzylic nitriles. The best match is mesitylacetonitrile. Integrals were not supplied, so proton counts were assigned from the structure (2+2+6+3 = 13)."
  },
